   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Hi all,</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I&#39;d like to advertise an auxiliary NIMBLE package, <b>nimbleEcology</b>. <br></span></div><div><p><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">nimbleEcology\r\n contains a set of distributions corresponding to some \r\ncommon ecological models. These distributions are implemented to \r\nintegrate over latent states in the model. It&#39;s designed to integrate \r\nsmoothly with NIMBLE model coding.</span></p><p><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">The following distributions are available:<tt><br></tt></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><tt>dOcc </tt> (occupancy model)</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><tt>dDynOcc </tt> (dynamic occupancy model)</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><tt>dHMM </tt> (hidden Markov model)</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><tt> dDHMM </tt> (dynamic hidden Markov model)</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><tt> dCJS </tt> (Cormack-Jolly-Seber or mark-recapture model)</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><tt> dNmixture </tt> (N-mixture model)</span></li></ul><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">nimbleEcology and its documentation are now available on <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/nimbleEcology/index.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/nimbleEcology/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244915218000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3P9oW2J9J8TJYEfc_yTisk\">CRAN</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/nimble-dev/nimbleEcology\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/nimble-dev/nimbleEcology&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244915218000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3M3OPsWqljQQBBISqYmPLL\">GitHub</a>.\r\n It was also discussed in the recent Ecol &amp; Evol paper &quot;One size \r\ndoes not fit all: Customizing MCMC methods for hierarchical models using\r\n NIMBLE&quot; (<a href=\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/ece3.6053\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/ece3.6053&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244915218000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0JbZFYKtMLzIfTlouWF5CH\">Ponisio et al., 2020</a>). See also <a href=\"https://r-nimble.org/nimbleecology-custom-nimble-distributions-for-ecologists\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://r-nimble.org/nimbleecology-custom-nimble-distributions-for-ecologists&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244915218000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2MiLl1HacDxTvo55ssrM-U\">this blog post</a> with example code on <a href=\"http://r-nimble.org\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r-nimble.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244915218000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0iog4f5ByyJPOVvtzhkHlj\">r-nimble.org</a>.<br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Thanks,</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Ben Goldstein</span></div></div></div>\r\n"
